			<div class="content" id="post-content-4854124">
									

<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;Open&nbsp;for&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>The first suit was tested, the U.S. army closed the deal off after they saw what horrible things the suit can do.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>What horrible things? There's kinda an implication that this can do many different things but I don't really have a feel for what.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Only 3 were made two are still lost and the third one a soldier still wears.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>What does 'lost' mean here? Like, 'missing'? Or 'destroyed'? If it's the first, why is no-one else looking for it?</p>
<hr />
<p>This feels&#8230;a little unsatisfying to me. On one level, there's some thematic weirdness: there's this like, sense that the SCP is a dude who just, wants to do his best and is a big dang hero that everyone loves, except the US army found it too horrifying to use and so there's this disconnect between the angle of 'the foundation will do anything and resort to any means' which feels kinda horrifying and the angle of this dude just being super nice and cool and chill, which feels kinda heartwarming.</p>
<p>On another level: you don't really do anything interesting with this; there's a long investigation section at the start that feels kinda uninteresting because none of the discoveries are particularly novel (since, the discovery would be after the description here: we already know the foundation found a suit and there's a person in it cos guess what, we already read the description) and then there's a vague thing about him joining an MTF. This isn't a bad thing to happen but it's under-utilised: there's no like, extensive training sequence and determined work by the SCP towards convincing the Foundation he can be helpful and uncertainty of whether he'd achieve that; but there's also no real like&#8230;cool things happening as a result of them being in a MTF; there's no 'mission log' or anything and I'm left feeling like this just&#8230;doesn't have the narrative meat to it for it to work.</p>
<p>Circling back to the themes: I'm really not a fan of the kinda, glorification of the military throughout this. This is, obviously, a personal thing but it's very possible that I just wouldn't like something this 'boo yah go soldiers' even if you had executed it well.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

