			<div class="content" id="post-content-4854118">
									

<p>Ok, so here's the problem I'm having right now with this particular project. I'm trying to stay within the template and within the word count. I'm trying not to reveal too much information because if I do, it might seem like a big mess or too much information for someone to swallow in one sitting. The James Devillian Twist SCP project is a big project. I mean&#8230; a very big project. He has a wide array of other anomalous abilities and somewhat complicated motivations. He doesn't see someone's destiny. He sees their &quot;supposed&quot; destiny, or what it is that they were meant to do in life, the thing that they are driven towards or driven to do. He sees this along with a ton of other information about that object, including any weaknesses they hold. Twist is a psychopath who will always know how to put his target down.</p>
<p>I read through 049. One major difference here is that through experimentation and interrogation, Twist's &quot;LLUN&quot; threat is verifiable and the second difference is its not a disease. Twist just thinks that if he introduces a small bit of the LLUN's nature to the world, that it might be able to prepare for the upcoming apocalyptic battle with the LLUN, similar to how a vaccine works in a way.</p>
<p>Should I do away with the template and try my own thing with presenting this concept? Use my own format? There isn't really a section in the template for SCP Abilities.</p>

							</div>

								
					
