<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-XXXX is a computer program that one day appeared and automatically installed in every computer at site-XX.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This feels&#8230;a little unsatisfying to me? Iunno, I like the idea of the program spreading through alternative universes and like, letting you control people in other universes, but it feels&#8230;purposeless?</p>
<p>I think at the end of the day, the lack of purpose is my biggest issue with this concept: there's some really cool flavour here and I like the idea of the Foundation eventually figuring out that it's not simulating stuff but it feels&#8230;like this is the setting of a story where you haven't managed to tease the core narrative arc out yet?</p>
<p>It feels like this needs&#8230;a character to focus on say, or for the plot of this to end up going somewhere more than just, revealing more about what this does. The idea of playing with the conflict between 'using this to figure out how to handle containment breaches better' and 'not using this to prevent it spreading and reduce the risk of a containment breach here' could be fun; or a discussion of the ethics of causing harm in another universe instead could be good; but without something like this where it ends up y'know, escalating and coming to some kinda conclusion, I'm not sure it'd work.</p>
</div>
</div>
