									</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/cybersqyd" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5336470); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5336470&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608990438" alt="cybersqyd" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5336470)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/cybersqyd" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5336470); return false;" >cybersqyd</a></span> <span class="odate time_1608982943 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">26 Dec 2020 11:42</span>
																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-89000/help:ideas-critique">Writing Help / Help: Ideas Critique</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13953701/seeking-greenlight-literally-just-straight-fucking-ice-zombi">(Seeking greenlight) Literally just straight fucking ice zombies</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4854051">
									

<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;Open&nbsp;for&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>that converts people into &quot;ice zombies&quot; using unknown means.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>What do you mean by 'ice zombie'? Like, beings made of ice that behave like zombies? Zombies who can control ice?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>After a bit a &quot;portal&quot; (not really sure what it's going to be) to that universe opens up, and the foundation sends a research team into it.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>My concern with this sentence is two fold: it's a passive unfolding of events, and I don't know what happens when the research team enters or why we care.</p>
<p>When I say 'it's a passive unfolding of events', what I mean is that there's nothing the Foundation are doing to try and achieve this, it's just, something which happens; which in turn means there's no 'will they succeed?' tension but there's also no narrative hook here because until this happens, there's no way to hint that this will happen.</p>
<p>On the flip side: there's no real indication of there being any consequences to this happening. It's like the culmination of the story, where we finally find out what is happening and the curtain is whipped back to reveal&#8230;nothing?</p>
<hr />
<p>Fundamentally, my concern with this pitch is that it starts out sounding like a kinda generic zombie story with a slight twist of ice being involved, and then, instead of playing with that further, some stuff happens and a whole other universe is dragged in. It kinda feels like this is adding more complexity to the idea and introducing new elements in an attempt to be interesting, whereas if you actually wanted to make this work, you'd figure out how to do something interesting with the elements you already have.</p>
<p>IMO: this needs a shift in focus. Either the focus is this weird spot where anomalous things appear, and the Foundation trying to figure out <em>why</em> and how to stop it before they accidentally create a portal to the other universe and we learn something important about why this happens; or the focus should be on the ice zombies and the Foundation trying to deal with them, and the whole 'other universe' angle should be dropped. I think either thing could work, but I think blending them together like this is going to be unsatisfying cos you're forced to have the start of your article be effectively a bait and switch.</p>
<p>If you do this though, you're really going to have to consider the growth of the story: what changes in our understanding between the start and the end; how do the characters involved change; how do our feelings about this change; how do you get from a to b to c in a way that keeps a reader on board and excited for the journey.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

							</div>

								
					
