				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/cybersqyd" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5336470); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5336470&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608990438" alt="cybersqyd" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5336470)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/cybersqyd" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5336470); return false;" >cybersqyd</a></span> <span class="odate time_1608982312 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">26 Dec 2020 11:31</span>
																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-89000/help:ideas-critique">Writing Help / Help: Ideas Critique</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13947701/the-inventor">The Inventor</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4854039">
									

<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;Open&nbsp;for&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>so he started to travel across world and he ended up in one of the sites of SCP Fundation.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>How did he like&#8230;just end up in one of the sites of the Foundation? Was this a deliberate effort on his part or did it just kinda happen?</p>
<hr />
<p>My core concern with this proposal is that the central narrative section falls into two pitfalls: it's extremely focussed on what the SCP does to the point where it doesn't even mention the Foundation; and it's also extremely flat.</p>
<p>The problem with the first is that a SCP article is written by the Foundation, which means that they're the POV character(s) for the story: it'll inevitably have to be told via the tests the foundation does, or the interviews they carry out, or the incident reports that they write, or via journal notes that they find; and so focussing so much on what the SCP is and what they do can be a mistake because it means the Foundation are just kinda&#8230;there?</p>
<p>The issue with the second is that there's no change throughout the story: it's expanding more on the context of The Inventor but a lot of this arc has happened already. Like, the inventor is ~4 billion years old, he's clearly come to terms with him having never run out of creativity, and so there's not really any growth? The Foundation doesn't learn to contain him better; there's no like, struggle from the inventor's aim being impossible; and so I'm left wanting more out of this.</p>
<p>I think this really could work and be an interesting story: I just think it needs you to figure out what the actual story within the article is. I feel like the most interesting angle is either the inventor coming to terms with his literal created purpose being impossible for him to complete; or for the foundation to attempt to utilise his inventiveness and then something happening as a result of this. At it's core, my issue is that this needs something interesting to happen with the pieces you've set up.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

